  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieved 0.485 accuracy, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (0.208), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the multiprofile setting (capturing multiple cell profiles per sample with aggregation) can further improve the RNA signal beyond the single-profile baseline. This experiment (config_002) tests that single conceptual change—multiprofile with avgpool aggregation—while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder and RNA-only model, giving a clean comparison against config_001. It is the best use of experiment 3 because it directly extends our strongest configuration with a minimal, interpretable modification; if multiprofile+avgpool helps, we can then explore transformer aggregation (config_003) or combine multiprofile with learned encoders (scvi, scgpt) in later experiments. If it doesn't help, we learn that the single-profile PCA representation is already near its ceiling and should pivot to testing better encoders (config_004/007) or a stronger image encoder (config_013) to inform whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile."
}

